# Shell scripts run on a Linux VPS, verbatim, however they get there —
# through a checkout, CI's own scp step, or a manual scp straight from a
# contributor's Windows working copy (see .scripts/provision/README.md's
# 2026-08-11 entry). A CRLF line ending breaks bash the moment it hits
# something quote-sensitive (e.g. `set -o pipefail`), regardless of the
# committer's own core.autocrlf setting — enforced here instead of relying
# on that per-machine config being right.
*.sh text eol=lf
